":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-53","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-53"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 40, lines 47-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 40, lines 47-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 33-43","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 33-43"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 72, lines 13-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 72, lines 13-13"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["the sides that brought the case argue the Ninth Circuit erred by failing to defer to the district court's factual determinations.","the opposing sides argue that de novo review is the proper standard for assessing prejudice in capital cases."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-53","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-53"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 40, lines 47-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 40, lines 47-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 33-43","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-982_m64n.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 33-43"},{"evidence